---
import { url } from "../lib/paths";
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import { topics } from "../data/topics";
---
<Page
  title="About Us"
  eyebrow="Our story"
  description="Tech for Grownups exists for one reason: to make technology feel friendly, clear and a little less frustrating."
>
  <h2>Why we started</h2>
  <p>
    Technology moves fast. Phones update overnight, buttons move, and the instructions you find online are often
    written by experts for other experts. Too many smart, capable adults end up feeling left behind, or relying on
    someone else every time something changes.
  </p>
  <p>
    We started Tech for Grownups to change that. Our goal is simple: <strong>clear, patient, step-by-step help</strong>
    that anyone can follow, no matter how comfortable they are with technology.
  </p>

  <h2>What makes our guides different</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Plain English.</strong> We avoid jargon. When a technical word is needed, we explain it.</li>
    <li><strong>One step at a time.</strong> Short steps, in order, with nothing skipped.</li>
    <li><strong>Pictures that help.</strong> Screenshots showing exactly where to tap or click.</li>
    <li><strong>Easy to read.</strong> Large text and a calm design, on any screen.</li>
    <li><strong>Always free.</strong> Every guide and cheat sheet is free to read and download.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we cover</h2>
  <p>We write guides for the devices and apps people use every day:</p>
  <ul>
    {topics.map((t) => <li><a href={url(`/topics/${t.slug}`)}>{t.name}</a>: {t.desc}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>How we keep guides accurate</h2>
  <p>
    We follow each guide step by step on real devices before publishing. Because phones and computers change with
    every update, we review our guides regularly and show the date each one was last updated. If you spot something
    that has changed, please <a href={url("/contact")}>let us know</a>. We truly appreciate it.
  </p>

  <h2>How the site is funded</h2>
  <p>
    Tech for Grownups is free for everyone. We cover our costs through advertising and, occasionally, affiliate links
    to products we recommend. This never affects our advice. You can read more in our
    <a href={url("/disclaimer")}>Disclaimer</a> and <a href={url("/privacy-policy")}>Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <div class="note">
    <p><strong>Have a question or an idea for a guide?</strong> We'd love to hear from you. Visit our <a href={url("/contact")}>Contact page</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Page>
